    <section class="journal-hero" aria-labelledby="journalHeroTitle">
      <div class="journal-hero-inner">
        <p class="journal-hero-eyebrow" data-i18n="journalHeroEyebrow">TOKAIDO SHINKANSEN WINDOW STAMPS</p>
        <h1 id="journalHeroTitle" data-i18n="journalHeroTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">Turn the views you find</span> <span class="copy-chunk">into digital stamps</span></h1>
        <p class="journal-hero-lead" data-i18n="journalHeroLead"><span class="copy-chunk">Like collecting station stamps,</span> <span class="copy-chunk">save Mt. Fuji, castles, lakes and signs from the Tokaido Shinkansen window.</span> <span class="copy-chunk">Make it a family spotting game</span> <span class="copy-chunk">or a journal for a solo ride.</span></p>
        <div class="journal-hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="en/start.html#journey" data-cta-track="journal_train_search_click" data-cta-id="journal-hero-train-search" data-i18n="journalHeroPrimary">Build my guide</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost journal-hero-secondary" href="en/journal.html#memories" data-cta-track="journal_stamp_board_click" data-cta-id="journal-hero-stamp-board" data-i18n="journalHeroSecondary">Collect window stamps</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost journal-hero-secondary" href="en/journal.html#eki-stamp" data-cta-track="journal_eki_stamp_click" data-cta-id="journal-hero-eki-stamp">Find eki stamps</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section journal-how" aria-labelledby="journalHowTitle">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="journalHowEyebrow">HOW IT WORKS</p>
        <h2 id="journalHowTitle" data-i18n="journalHowTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">Find it, record it,</span> <span class="copy-chunk">grow the journey</span></h2>
        <p class="section-sub" data-i18n="journalHowSub">Choose your train before you ride, then record the views you spot from the window.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="journal-step-grid">
        <article class="journal-step">
          <span class="journal-step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalStep1Title">Choose a train and next view</h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalStep1Body">Pick a train to open a window timeline for your direction.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-step">
          <span class="journal-step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalStep2Title">Spot it and mark it seen</h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalStep2Body">When a view appears outside, tap its stamp to record the moment.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-step">
          <span class="journal-step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalStep3Title">Collect stamps and grow medals</h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalStep3Body">Your recorded views stay on the stamp board, building progress across each medal series.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="journal-how-actions">
        <a class="inline-cta" href="en/journal.html#stampboard" data-cta-track="journal_stamp_board_click" data-cta-id="journal-howto-stamp-board"><span data-i18n="journalHowCta">Open the stamp board</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section journal-board-section" id="memories">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="memEyebrow">YOUR WINDOW STAMP JOURNAL</p>
        <h2 data-i18n="memTitle">Window Stamps &amp; Medals</h2>
        <p class="section-sub" data-i18n="memSub">Record the views you find and watch your journey take shape.</p>
        <p class="journal-intro" data-i18n="journalIntro">Keep the Mt. Fuji, castles, lakes and signs you spot from the Tokaido Shinkansen as Window Stamps.</p>
        <p class="journal-intro" id="journal-save-help">Save views you want to see with the star in the <a href="en/zukan.html#gallery">window view gallery</a>. Use stamps to record views you have spotted.</p>
        <p class="journal-intro" id="journal-storage-help">Favorites and stamps are saved in this browser. In the Android app, they are saved within the app. They do not sync automatically between the app, browsers or devices.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="medal-board" id="medalBoard" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <h3 class="stamp-heading" data-i18n="stampHeading">All stamps</h3>
      <div class="stampboard" id="stampboard"></div>
      <div class="journal-collection-grid" aria-label="Themed collections">
        <a class="journal-collection-card" href="en/727-collection.html">
          <div class="journal-collection-thumb">
            <img src="images/thumbs/20260820_727_board_yoda_solo_3x_michikusa.webp" alt="A red-and-white 727 Cosmetics billboard standing across rice fields in Fujisawa" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </div>
          <div class="journal-collection-body">
            <p class="eyebrow">727 COLLECTION</p>
            <h3>Collect 727 signs</h3>
            <p>Track individual billboard locations and milestone medals on the dedicated guide.</p>
            <span class="journal-collection-cta">Explore collection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="journal-collection-card" href="en/ferris-wheels.html">
          <div class="journal-collection-thumb">
            <img src="images/thumbs/20260824_hirakata_park_wheel_michikusa.webp" alt="The Hirakata Park Ferris wheel lit at dusk from the Shinkansen window" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </div>
          <div class="journal-collection-body">
            <p class="eyebrow">FERRIS WHEELS</p>
            <h3>Collect ferris wheels</h3>
            <p>Explore the little wheels along the route in a separate field guide.</p>
            <span class="journal-collection-cta">Explore collection <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="journal-intro" id="journal-reset-help">Resetting removes both your stamps and your favorites.</p>
      <div class="mem-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-small" id="resetBtn" data-i18n="btnReset">Reset stamps</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="journal-afterboard" aria-labelledby="journalUsesTitle">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="journalUsesEyebrow">FIND YOUR WAY TO COLLECT</p>
        <h2 id="journalUsesTitle" data-i18n="journalUsesTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">One collection,</span> <span class="copy-chunk">different kinds of journey</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="journal-use-grid">
        <article class="journal-use-card">
          <span class="journal-use-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalFamilyTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">A window game</span> <span class="copy-chunk">for family trips</span></h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalFamilyBody">Ask “What will we see next?” and look for scenery together, then record the moment as a stamp.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-use-card">
          <span class="journal-use-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalSoloTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">A travel journal</span> <span class="copy-chunk">for solo rides</span></h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalSoloBody">Keep the Fuji, castles and lakes you meet along the way, at your own pace.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-use-card">
          <span class="journal-use-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <h3 data-i18n="journalStationTitle"><span class="copy-chunk">A moving collection</span> <span class="copy-chunk">for station-stamp fans</span></h3>
          <p data-i18n="journalStationBody">If you love collecting paper eki stamps at stations, try gathering scenery between stations as a different kind of travel collection.</p>
          <a class="journal-eki-jump" href="en/journal.html#eki-stamp">Find eki stamps <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <div class="journal-after-actions">
        <a class="inline-cta journal-zukan-cta" href="en/zukan.html" data-cta-track="journal_zukan_click" data-cta-id="journal-use-cases-zukan"><span data-i18n="journalZukanCta">Browse the window field guide</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section journal-eki-section" id="eki-stamp" aria-labelledby="journalEkiTitle">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">REAL EKI STAMPS</p>
        <h2 id="journalEkiTitle">Paper eki stamps at the station</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">Many Japanese stations keep a commemorative rubber stamp ("eki stamp") depicting the station building or local landmarks. Collect digital window stamps while you ride, and press paper eki stamps before you board or after you step off.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="journal-eki-grid">
        <article class="journal-eki-card">
          <div class="journal-eki-card-head">
            <h3>Tokyo Station</h3>
            <span class="journal-eki-badge is-out">Outside gates</span>
          </div>
          <p class="journal-eki-where">JR East · Outside Marunouchi South Exit</p>
          <p class="journal-eki-body">Features the Marunouchi Station Building and Silver Bell. There is no permanent stamp inside the Shinkansen gates—head to the red-brick Marunouchi side before departure or after arrival.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-eki-card">
          <div class="journal-eki-card-head">
            <h3>Kyoto Station</h3>
            <span class="journal-eki-badge is-local">Inside local gates</span>
          </div>
          <p class="journal-eki-where">JR West · Inside conventional-line gates (near Central / West Exits)</p>
          <p class="journal-eki-body">Features the Kyoto Station Building and Kyoto Tower. Located on the JR West local-line side rather than the Shinkansen concourse—handy when transferring or exiting.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-eki-card">
          <div class="journal-eki-card-head">
            <h3>Shin-Osaka Station</h3>
            <span class="journal-eki-badge is-counter">Local ticket counter</span>
          </div>
          <p class="journal-eki-where">JR West · East Gate counter (ask staff) or near the East Exit ticket office</p>
          <p class="journal-eki-body">Sometimes kept behind the counter on request. JR Central does not keep a permanent stamp on the Shinkansen side, except during limited-time campaigns.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="journal-eki-card is-none">
          <div class="journal-eki-card-head">
            <h3>Nagoya Station</h3>
            <span class="journal-eki-badge is-none">No permanent stamp</span>
          </div>
          <p class="journal-eki-where">No permanent JR station stamp</p>
          <p class="journal-eki-body">Most JR Central Tokaido Shinkansen stations do not keep permanent stamps; Nagoya Station generally offers them only during limited-time stamp rallies.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="journal-eki-note">Bring a notebook or blank paper for a clean impression. Stamp locations and availability can change without notice—ask station staff if you cannot find one.<span class="journal-eki-src">Sources (Japanese, checked Nov 2026): <a href="https://stamp.funakiya.com/jr-tokyo.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tokyo</a> · <a href="https://stamp.funakiya.com/jr-kyoto.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kyoto</a> · <a href="https://stamp.funakiya.com/jr-shinosaka.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Shin-Osaka</a> · <a href="https://stamp.funakiya.com/jr-nagoya.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nagoya</a> (Tabi no Stamp-cho)</span></p>
    </section>
